      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using an everything-scoped codesearch for:\n`GOOGLE_JAVA_FORMAT_PATH` and `f:google-java-format/google-java-format$`, I don\u0027t see anything other than a chromium derivative.\n\ngoogle-java-format does not come with a wrapper script. The wrapper script that depot_tools looks for here is the one that I wrote in chromium. Projects can use their own custom wrapper scripts to set options.\n\nThe chromium wrapper script does allow options via `GOOGLE_JAVA_FORMAT_ARGS`: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/google-java-format/google-java-format?ss\u003dchromium\u0026q\u003dgoogle-java-format\n\nFor reference, here\u0027s what works in R8\u0027s repo:\nhttps://r8-review.git.corp.google.com/c/r8/+/112160",
